{"id":"92112d97-bb64-4b44-86f2-ea5691ef8f6e","revision":0,"last_node_id":133,"last_link_id":222,"nodes":[{"id":97,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[-750,830],"size":[610,853.984375],"flags":{},"order":0,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"properties":{"ue_properties":{"widget_ue_connectable":{},"version":"7.7","input_ue_unconnectable":{}}},"widgets_values":["## How to use this workflow\n\n1. **Load your image** into the LoadImage node.\n2. **Right-click** the LoadImage node \u2192 **Open in MaskEditor**.\n3. **Paint over the person you want to KEEP**. Anything you don't paint will be regenerated by Klein based on the prompt.\n4. Save the mask (button in the MaskEditor).\n5. In the Klein subgraph, edit the **prompt** (e.g. \"remove all the people from this photo\").\n6. Optionally adjust **megapixels** (1 = 1024\u00d71024 area, 4 = 2048\u00d72048 area).\n7. Run.\n\nThe output is saved as **`Flux2-Klein-FaceProtect_xxxxx_.png`** in your ComfyUI output directory.\n\n### How it works\n\n- Klein processes the full image and removes all people per the prompt.\n- The painted area is then composited back from the original image, restoring the person you wanted to keep.\n- An `InvertMask` node handles ComfyUI's mask convention (painted = 0 in the MASK output) so you can paint naturally over what you want to preserve.\n\n---\n\n## Model Links (for Local Users)\n\n**diffusion_models**\n\n- [flux-2-klein-base-9b-fp8.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-klein-base-9b-fp8)\n\n> Please visit BFL's repo, accept the agreement in the repo, and then download the fp8 model.\n\n**text_encoders**\n\n- [qwen_3_8b_fp8mixed.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/flux2-klein-9B/resolve/main/split_files/text_encoders/qwen_3_8b_fp8mixed.safetensors)\n\n**vae**\n\n- [full_encoder_small_decoder.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-small-decoder/resolve/main/full_encoder_small_decoder.safetensors)\n\n\n## Model Storage Location\n\n```\n\ud83d\udcc2 ComfyUI/\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 \ud83d\udcc2 models/\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 \ud83d\udcc2 diffusion_models/\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 flux-2-klein-base-9b-fp8.safetensors\n\u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 \ud83d\udcc2 text_encoders/\n\u2502   \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 qwen_3_8b_fp8mixed.safetensors\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 \ud83d\udcc2 vae/\n\u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 full_encoder_small_decoder.safetensors\n```\n\n## Report Issue\n\nNote: Please update ComfyUI first ([guide](https://docs.comfy.org/installation/update_comfyui)) and prepare required models. Desktop/Cloud updates follow stable releases, so some nightly-supported models may not be available yet.\n\n- Cannot run / runtime errors: [ComfyUI/issues](https://github.com/comfyanonymous/ComfyUI/issues)\n- UI / frontend issues: [ComfyUI_frontend/issues](https://github.com/Comfy-Org/ComfyUI_frontend/issues)\n- Workflow issues: [workflow_templates/issues](https://github.com/Comfy-Org/workflow_templates/issues)\n"],"color":"#222","bgcolor":"#000"},{"id":99,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[470,650],"size":[230,120],"flags":{},"order":1,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"Note","properties":{"ue_properties":{"widget_ue_connectable":{},"version":"7.7","input_ue_unconnectable":{}}},"widgets_values":["The node below is a subgraph. Learn more at [Subgraph docs](https://docs.comfy.org/interface/features/subgraph)"],"color":"#222","bgcolor":"#000"},{"id":75,"type":"7b34ab90-36f9-45ba-a665-71d418f0df18","pos":[309.99977373615457,829.9999230401296],"size":[400,470],"flags":{},"order":3,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"name":"unet_name","type":"COMBO","widget":{"name":"unet_name"},"link":null},{"name":"clip_name","type":"COMBO","widget":{"name":"clip_name"},"link":null},{"name":"vae_name","type":"COMBO","widget":{"name":"vae_name"},"link":null},{"label":"prompt","name":"text","type":"STRING","widget":{"name":"text"},"link":null},{"name":"image","type":"IMAGE","link":155},{"name":"megapixels","type":"FLOAT","widget